hadiths[26]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2090","Jabir bin 'Abdullah said:\The wife of Sa'd bin Ar-Rabi came with her two daughters from Sa'd to he Messenger of Allah(S.A.W)and said; O Messenger of Allah(S.A.W)! these two are daughters of Sa'd bin Ar-Rabi who fought along with you on the day of Uhud and was martyred. Their uncle took their wealth"""""
"2091","Huzail bin Shurahbil said:\A man came to Abu Musa and Salman bin Rabiah and asked them about a daughter"""""
"2092","Al-Harith narrated that 'Ali said:\You recite this ayah: After payment of legacies he(or she) may have bequeathed or debts"""""
"2093","Al-Harith narrated that 'Ali said:\The Messenger of Allah(S.A.W) judged that the children (sons and daughters) from the same mother and father inherit"""""
"2094","Jabir bin 'Abdullah said:\The Messenger of Allah(S.A.W) came to visit me while I was ill at Banu Salamah. I said : 'O Prophet of Allah(S.A.W)! How shall I divide my wealth among my children?' But he did not say anything to me"""""
"2095","Narrated by Ahmad ibn Mani', narrated by Yazid ibn Harun, from Abu Ghassan, Muhammad ibn Mutarrif, from Hassan ibn Atiyyah, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), who said: \Modesty (al-hayā') and reticence (al-'iyy) are two branches of faith (īmān)"","" while obscenity (al-badhā') and excessive eloquence (al-bayān) are two branches of hypocrisy (nifāq).\""\n\nAbu 'Isa (al-Tirmidhī) said: \""This is a hasan gharīb hadith; we know it only from the narration of Abu Ghassan Muhammad ibn Mutarrif.\"" He further explained: \""Al-'iyy refers to speaking little"","" al-badhā' means obscenity in speech"","" and al-bayān refers to excessive speech—such as those orators who deliver sermons"","" expanding their words and displaying eloquence in them"","" praising people in ways that do not please Allah.\"""""""
"2096","Ibn 'Abbas narrated that the Messenger of Allah(S.A.W) said:\Give the shares of inheritance to those who are entitled to them. As for what remains"""""
"2097","Imran bin Husain narrated:\A man came to the Prophet (S.A.W) and said\"" 'My son died"""""
"2098","Qabisah bin Dhuw'aib said:\A grandmother - the mother of a mother"""""
"2099","Qabisah bin Dhuw'aib said:\A grandmother came to Abu Bakr to ask him about her inheritance. He said to her"""""
"2100","Yahya ibn Aktham and al-Jarud ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, both saying: al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated to us; al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us, from Awf ibn Dahlam, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar رضي الله عنهما, who said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah ﷺ ascended the pulpit and called out in a loud voice, saying:\n\n*\O assembly of those who have submitted with their tongues but whose faith has not yet reached their hearts: do not harm the Muslims"","" do not reproach them"","" and do not seek out their faults. For whoever seeks out the faults of his Muslim brother"","" Allah shall seek out his faults; and whoever has Allah seek out his faults"","" He shall expose him"","" even if he were in the innermost part of his home.\""*\n\nIbn 'Umar رضي الله عنهما said: \""One day he looked at the House (i.e."","" the Ka'bah) and said: *'How great you are"","" and how great is your sanctity! Yet the believer is of greater sanctity before Allah than you.'*\""\n\nAbu 'Isa (al-Tirmidhī) said: \""This is a *hasan gharīb* hadith. We know it only through the narration of al-Husayn ibn Waqid. Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm al-Samarqandī also narrated something similar from al-Husayn ibn Waqid"","" and a similar narration has been reported from Abū Barzah al-Aslamī رضي الله عنه from the Prophet ﷺ.\"""""""
"2101","Abu Umamah bin Sahl bin Hunaif said:\'Umar bin Al-Khattab sent me with a letter to Abu'Ubaidah (saying) that The Messenger of Allah(S.A.W) said : 'Allah and His Messenger are responsible for the one who has no patron. And the maternal uncle inherits from the one who has no heirs"""""
"2102","'Ali ibn Hujr narrated to us: Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from 'Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), who said: \Whoever is given a gift and has the means"","" let him reciprocate with it. If he does not have the means"","" let him praise the giver. For whoever praises has shown gratitude"","" and whoever conceals the favor has been ungrateful. And whoever adorns himself with what he was not given is like one wearing garments of falsehood.\"" Abu 'Isa said: This is a hasan gharib hadith. There are also narrations on this topic from Asma' bint Abi Bakr and 'Aishah (may Allah be pleased with them). The meaning of his statement"","" \""Whoever conceals has been ungrateful"",""\"" is that he has denied the blessing."""""
"2103","al-Husayn ibn al-Hasan al-Marwazi narrated to us in Makkah, and Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us, saying: al-Ahwas ibn Jawwab narrated to us, from Su'ayr ibn al-Khims, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Abu 'Uthman al-Nahdi, from Usamah ibn Zayd (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Whoever is done a favor and says to the one who did it"","" 'Jazak Allahu khairan' (May Allah reward you with good)"","" has indeed expressed the highest praise.\"" Abu 'Isa said: This is a hasan jayyid gharib hadith. We do not know of it from the hadith of Usamah ibn Zayd except through this chain. It has also been narrated from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) with a similar wording. I asked Muhammad (i.e."","" al-Bukhari) about it"","" but he did not know it.\n\n'Abd al-Rahim ibn Hazim al-Balkhi narrated to me"","" saying: I heard al-Maki ibn Ibrahim say: We were with Ibn Jurayj al-Maki when a beggar came and asked him for help. Ibn Jurayj said to his treasurer"","" \""Give him a dinar.\"" The treasurer replied"","" \""I only have one dinar; if I give it"","" I and my family will go hungry.\"" Ibn Jurayj became angry and said"","" \""Give it to him.\"" Al-Maki said: While we were with Ibn Jurayj"","" a man came with a letter and a purse. A brother of his had sent him"","" and in the letter it was written: \""I have sent you fifty dinars.\"" Ibn Jurayj opened the purse and counted them"","" and they were fifty-one dinars. He then said to his treasurer: \""You gave one"","" and Allah has returned it to you and added fifty more.\"""""""
"2104","Aishah narrated that a freed slave of the Prophet (s.a.w) fell from foliage on a date-palm and died. So the Prophet (S.A.W) said:\See if he has any heirs.\"" They said: \""No.\"" He said: 'Pay it to someone among the people of the town"""""
"2105","Ibn 'Abbas narrated that :a man died during the time of the Messenger of Allah(S.A.W)"
"2106","Usamah bin Zaid narrated that the Messenger of Allah(S.A.W) said:\The Muslim does not inherit from the disbeliever"""""
"2107","Jabir narrated that the Prophet(S.A.W) said:\The people of two religions do not inherit from each other"""""
"2108","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Prophet(S.A.W) said:\The murderer will not inherit"""""
"2109","Sa'eed bin Al-Musayyab said:\'Umar said: 'The blood-money is upon the 'Aqilah"""""
"2110","Abu Hurairah narrated that :the Messenger of Allah(S.A.W) judged the payment of a Gurrah male or female slave in the case of a woman's fetus from Banu Libyan which miscarried. Then the woman who was required to give the Gurrah died"
"2111","Abudullah bin Mawhab - and some of them said- 'Abdullah bin Wahb"
"2112","Narrated by Mahmud ibn Ghaylan, who said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from al-A'mash, who said: I heard Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said:\n\n> *\Whoever kills himself with an iron instrument"","" his iron instrument shall be in his hand"","" and he shall stab himself in the belly with it in the Fire of Jahannam"","" abiding therein forever and ever. And whoever kills himself with poison"","" his poison shall be in his hand"","" and he shall sip it in the Fire of Jahannam"","" abiding therein forever and ever. And whoever throws himself from a mountain and kills himself"","" he shall be falling in the Fire of Jahannam"","" abiding therein forever and ever.\""*\n\nNarrated by Muhammad ibn al-'Ala'"","" who said: Waqi' and Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us"","" from al-A'mash"","" from Abu Salih"","" from Abu Hurayrah"","" from the Prophet ﷺ"","" with a narration similar to the hadith of Shu'bah from al-A'mash.\n\nAbu 'Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: *\""This hadith is sahih"","" and it is more authentic than the first hadith.\""* Thus narrated more than one narrator this hadith from al-A'mash"","" from Abu Salih"","" from Abu Hurayrah"","" from the Prophet ﷺ.\n\nMuhammad ibn 'Ajlan narrated from Sa'id al-Maqburi"","" from Abu Hurayrah"","" from the Prophet ﷺ"","" who said:\n\n> *\""Whoever kills himself with poison shall be punished in the Fire of Jahannam.\""*\n\nAnd he did not mention in it: *\""abiding therein forever and ever.\""* And thus narrated Abu al-Zinad"","" from al-A'raj"","" from Abu Hurayrah"","" from the Prophet ﷺ. And this is more authentic"","" because the narrations generally come with the understanding that the people of Tawhid (monotheism) are punished in the Fire and then taken out of it"","" and it is not mentioned that they abide therein eternally."""""
"2113","Suwayd ibn Nasr narrated to us, saying: 'Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak informed us from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, from Mujahid, from Abu Hurayrah, who said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, forbade the use of foul medicine.\n\nAbu Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: \He meant poison.\"""""""
"2114","Wathilah bin Al-Asqa' narrated that the Messenger of Allah(S.A.W) said:\The woman collects three inheritance: Whomever she freed"""""
"2115","Muhammad ibn Maddawayh narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ḥammād al-Shuʿaythī narrated to us, saying: ʿAbbād ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allāh be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Indeed"","" the best of remedies you have are snuff (al-saʿūṭ)"","" a drink administered for throat ailments (al-ladūd)"","" cupping (al-ḥijāmah)"","" and walking (al-mashy).\""\n\nWhen the Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) fell ill"","" his Companions administered the throat remedy (al-ladūd) to him. When they had finished"","" he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""Administer it to them (as well).\"" So they all received the treatment except al-ʿAbbās (may Allāh be pleased with him)."""""
